ation.\n\nLine $L4$ follows from the fact that {{field-4}} matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a016197-61af-57f3-9c3a-05410db1374d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Inexact Differential Equations Using Integrating Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e958fa7a-2530-5e28-9195-e3dd1010f6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216604} {:answer/id #uuid "0c1ef443-4597-541d-a8b8-ab8eac9b4807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216605} {:answer/id #uuid "331ca236-b1f1-5b54-9bf6-4ef67cedef79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216606} {:answer/id #uuid "64939ccc-a9bb-5407-afbc-0c31373b00bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216607}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7b6ed42b-5c85-5ddb-bee9-efa742312304" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f23ef2ff-c615-5327-8856-dcaefed546c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}y^{4} + 3x^{2}y^{2} + xy = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216609} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9098f4-a6d7-59b2-aa95-8e2743fc9f5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}y^{3} + 2x^{3}y^{2} + y = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216610} {:answer/id #uuid "139036de-8f75-5274-bd83-8a15afa69a21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}y^{3} + 2xy^{2} + y = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216611} {:answer/id #uuid "1ffffdcd-1009-542a-b618-7670fe4f7c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}y^{2} + xy^{2} + xy = c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216612}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5ccc11c6-641b-5db3-a990-fccf006a1b53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186216608}] :question/id #uuid "1effee9c-dd60-525b-b725-817b354982d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-337096" :question/problem "Consider the inexact differential equation\n$(\\frac{6y^{2}}{x} + 4y^{3})dx + (4y + 3xy^{2} + \\frac{1}{x^{3}})dy = 0$.\nIt is known that\n$\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y} - \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) = \\frac{3}{x}$\nwhere the functions $P$ and $Q$ are given by\n\n$P(x, y) = \\frac{6y^{2}}{x} + 4y^{3}, Q(x, y) = 4y + 3xy^{2} + \\frac{1}{x^{3}}$.\n\nUse this information to find a suitable integrating factor $I(x)$ and hence find the general solution to the equation.\n\nA suitable integrating factor is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is {{field-2}}, where $c$ is a constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c60eb52-e275-5f9e-8b64-8f24c6fbbbff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2\\cos^{2} 2t + 3\\sin^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117778} {:answer/id #uuid "5068c443-8395-505c-92d8-71cea0dfc17e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4\\cos^{2} 2t + 9\\sin^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117779} {:answer/id #uuid "748e7d72-d682-5524-af39-e923fed4a5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4\\sin^{2} 2t + 9\\cos^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117780} {:answer/id #uuid "7997a0c6-f7e9-5d98-aedd-32f939d3e168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2\\sin^{2} 2t + 9\\cos^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117781} {:answer/id #uuid "7eb306df-b1bd-5be5-b18b-0285d0ccf69e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/v